            <div xml:id="d375">

                <pb facs="0387" n="375" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg375"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/3963: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Lithuania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Norem</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kaunas</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-06-18T14:00:00+01:00">June 18, 1940—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:43 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>119. Occupation movements continue with Soviet units being moved towards German
                    border. Estimated number of Russian troops 300,000. Populace remains quietly at
                    work. Banks report normal turnover. Rumors of German concentrations seem well
                    substantiated. Jewish inhabitants moving away from western cities.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Moscow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Norem</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
